HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppppppooee device first appeared in OpenBSD 3.7.

BBUUGGSS
     This implementation is client side only.

     It is important to specify “netmask 255.255.255.255” to ifconfig(8).  If
     the netmask is unspecified, it will be set to 8 when 0.0.0.0 is config‐
     ured to the interface, and it will persist after negotiation.

     The presence of a mygate(5) file will interfere with the routing table.
     Make sure this file is either empty or does not exist.

     Two ppppppooee interfaces configured with the same wildcard destination ad‐
     dress cannot share a routing table.

